<title>USA: U.S. 3-year note auction average 5.879 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 3-year note auction average 5.879 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its auction of 3-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 3-YEAR NOTES DUE NOV 15, 1999</p>
<p>			     $18.501 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> LOW	 5.872    Awarded At	100.008     5-7/8</p>
<p> HIGH	5.889    High Yield	 99.962     Percent</p>
<p> AVERAGE   5.879    10 Percent	 99.989</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.28 Times</p>
<p>	   Tail -- (High Minus Average Yield) =  1   Basis Pts</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 15.Nov.99</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    3-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 15.Nov.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 05.Nov.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  18.501 BLN USD		 CUSIP    912827Z96</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   42.195			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   564.00 MLN			AUCTION AVERAGES</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 5.875</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.635 BLN		     PRICE	 99.989</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    5.889-5.872 PCT		YIELD	  5.879</p>
<p>AVERAGE YIELD DOWN FROM 6.118 PCT AT AUCTION ON 06.AUG.96</p>
<p>AVG YIELD LOWEST SINCE 5.043 PCT AT AUCTION ON 06.FEB.96</p>
